**What the benchmarks tell us and what to watch:**

| Metric | Why it matters | Red flag |
|---|---|---|
| **Parse throughput (ops/s)** by endpoint count | Config reload on SIGHUP must be fast. If parse takes >10ms you'll pause delivery. | >5ms for 50 endpoints |
| **p99 latency** | GC pauses during parse show up here. | p99 > 3× p50 |
| **Error-path throughput** | Broken configs must not be slower than valid ones (DoS via bad config). | Error path >2× slower than happy path |
| **Strict mode overhead** | Extra key-set iteration. Should be <10% overhead. | >20% regression |
| **Memory per config** | Configs are long-lived (held in `ConfigLoader.lastGood`). | >10 KiB for 10-endpoint config |

Run benchmarks in CI with `--expose-gc` and a baseline file. Fail the build on >15% regression from the stored baseline (prevents accidental quadratic loops in the parser).

